## Voice Pipeline Flow
1. Flutter captures audio via ffmpeg (16kHz mono s16le)
2. VAD detects speech (energy threshold 400, 3-frame start, 25-frame silence end)
3. Audio WAV sent as `voice_chunk` over WebSocket
4. Backend STT (Whisper tiny, GPU if available)
5. Command registry regex match → if matched, execute + quick response
6. If no regex match → LLM parse via `llm_parse_command` (llama3.2)
7. If no command → full voice pipeline (STT → LLM → TTS)
8. Known commands skip LLM entirely via `COMMAND_RESPONSES` dict
9. TTS runs in parallel with command execution via `asyncio.gather`

